  "headline": "Karthigai Deepam Lit At Thiruparankundram Following Court Mandate",
  "seoTitle": "Thiruparankundram Karthigai Deepam Lit Under Court…",
  "metaDescription": "The Karthigai Deepam was lit at the Thiruparankundram hill pillar under Supreme Court-mandated security and supervision by appointed retired judges.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "The Karthigai Deepam was successfully lit at the Thiruparankundram hill's stone pillar under strict security protocols.",
    "The ceremony proceeded under the oversight of two retired Madras High Court judges designated as receivers by the Supreme Court.",
    "Central Reserve Police Force personnel were deployed to secure the hillock to ensure compliance with the court's earlier directives."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The ritual of lighting the Karthigai Deepam at the Thiruparankundram hill occurred following an explicit order from the Supreme Court of India. The proceedings were overseen by retired Madras High Court Justices S. Vaidyanathan and V. Parthiban, who were appointed as receivers for the Arulmigu Subramaniya Swamy Temple. Security was managed by the Central Reserve Police Force to maintain order during the event. The ceremony took place amid broader legal and political discussions regarding the administration of the site, with the Supreme Court having previously issued contempt notices to various officials. Devotees gathered to witness the lighting, which was accompanied by traditional religious chants. Political discourse surrounding the event included statements from national party leaders following the judicial intervention in the site's management and the scheduling of the traditional lighting ceremony.",
